=== How to use ===
1. Create the Dataverse table with the columns title, description, priority (choice with values 100000000, 100000001, 100000002), requesteremail, conversationid and an autonumber column ticketnumber. Use your own publisher prefix instead of contoso_.
2. Create the flow inside a solution. In Copilot Studio open the topic, select Add node > Add a tool, pick this published flow (it appears as an Action node) and map the inputs in the order of the schema.
3. Always publish the agent after changing flow inputs or outputs; the topic keeps the old binding until you re-select the flow.
4. In the topic, add a condition: if ticketnumber equals ERROR, send an apology and offer the escalation topic.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Returning HTTP status 500 from the failure branch. The agent then reports a generic flow error; a normal 200 with a marker value gives you control of the message.
- Using the display name of a choice instead of its integer value in Dataverse actions.
- Reading the autonumber from a different action. The value only exists in the output of the Add a new row action (operation CreateRecord), not in the trigger.
- Running the flow with the author's connection for everyone. Row ownership and audit show the connection owner; use a service account on purpose.
- Long processing. The agent waits for the response, so keep the flow below about 30 seconds.

=== Testing ===
- Run the flow in the editor with a manual test and sample values, then test again from the Copilot Studio test panel.
- Rename the Dataverse table in the action to a wrong value to see the failure response.
- Check that Critical tickets reach the on-call channel and others do not.

The reference structure for production flows. All risky actions live in the Try scope. The Catch scope runs only if Try failed or timed out; it uses result('Try') to find the failing action and its error message, builds a deep link to the run with workflow(), notifies operations and then terminates the run as Failed, so that the run history and any monitoring still show the error. The example calls a health endpoint with an exponential retry policy.

=== Flow definition (JSON) ===
{
  "properties": {
    "connectionReferences": {
      "shared_office365": {
        "runtimeSource": "embedded",
        "connection": {
          "connectionReferenceLogicalName": "contoso_sharedoffice365_a1b2c"
        },
        "api": {
          "name": "shared_office365"
        }
      }
    },
    "definition": {
      "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Logic/schemas/2016-06-01/workflowdefinition.json#",
      "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
      "parameters": {
        "$connections": {
          "defaultValue": {},
          "type": "Object"
        },
        "$authentication": {
          "defaultValue": {},
          "type": "SecureObject"
        },
        "OpsMailbox (contoso_OpsMailbox)": {
          "defaultValue": "flow-alerts@contoso.example",
          "type": "String",
          "metadata": {
            "schemaName": "contoso_OpsMailbox"
          }
        }
      },
      "triggers": {
        "Every_hour": {
          "type": "Recurrence",
          "recurrence": {
            "frequency": "Hour",
            "interval": 1
          }
        }
      },
      "actions": {
        "Try": {
          "type": "Scope",
          "runAfter": {},
          "actions": {
            "Call_status_API": {
              "type": "Http",
              "runAfter": {},
              "inputs": {
                "method": "GET",
                "uri": "https://status.contoso.example/api/health",
                "headers": {
                  "Accept": "application/json"
                },
                "retryPolicy": {
                  "type": "exponential",
                  "count": 3,
                  "interval": "PT20S",
                  "minimumInterval": "PT10S",
                  "maximumInterval": "PT5M"
                }
              }
            },
            "Store_status": {
              "type": "Compose",
              "runAfter": {
                "Call_status_API": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": "@body('Call_status_API')"
            }
          }
        },
        "Catch": {
          "type": "Scope",
          "runAfter": {
            "Try": [
              "Failed",
              "TimedOut"
            ]
          },
          "actions": {
            "Failed_actions": {
              "type": "Query",
              "runAfter": {},
              "inputs": {
                "from": "@result('Try')",
                "where": "@or(equals(item()?['status'], 'Failed'), equals(item()?['status'], 'TimedOut'))"
              }
            },
            "Error_text": {
              "type": "Compose",
              "runAfter": {
                "Failed_actions": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": "@coalesce(first(body('Failed_actions'))?['error']?['message'], 'No error message available')"
            },
            "Run_link": {
              "type": "Compose",
              "runAfter": {
                "Error_text": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": "@concat('https://make.powerautomate.com/environments/', workflow()?['tags']?['environmentName'], '/flows/', workflow()?['name'], '/runs/', workflow()?['run']?['name'])"
            },
            "Mail_failure": {
              "type": "OpenApiConnection",
              "inputs": {
                "host": {
                  "connectionName": "shared_office365",
                  "operationId": "SendEmailV2",
                  "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_office365"
                },
                "parameters": {
                  "emailMessage/To": "@parameters('OpsMailbox (contoso_OpsMailbox)')",
                  "emailMessage/Subject": "@concat('Flow failed: ', workflow()?['tags']?['flowDisplayName'])",
                  "emailMessage/Body": "@concat('<p><b>Failed action:</b> ', first(body('Failed_actions'))?['name'], '</p><p><b>Error:</b> ', outputs('Error_text'), '</p><p><b>Time (UTC):</b> ', utcNow(), '</p><p><a href=\"', outputs('Run_link'), '\">Open the failed run</a></p>')",
                  "emailMessage/Importance": "High"
                },
                "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
              },
              "runAfter": {
                "Run_link": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              }
            },
            "Fail_the_run": {
              "type": "Terminate",
              "runAfter": {
                "Mail_failure": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": {
                "runStatus": "Failed",
                "runError": {
                  "code": "TryScopeFailed",
                  "message": "@outputs('Error_text')"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "schemaVersion": "1.0.0.0"
}

=== How to use ===
1. Copy the Try and Catch scopes into your own flow and move your actions into Try.
2. Create an environment variable OpsMailbox, or replace the parameter with a shared mailbox or Teams channel post.
3. Keep the Terminate action at the end of Catch. Without it the run shows Succeeded, because the Catch scope handled the error.
4. Optionally copy the pattern into a child flow, so that all flows share one error notification.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Not setting runAfter on the Catch scope for Failed and TimedOut. The default Succeeded condition never fires in the error case.
- Forgetting that result() only returns the direct children of the scope. For nested actions, filter the nested result as well.
- Using workflow()?['run']?['name'] outside a real run. In the editor test with sample data the value can be empty.
- Sending the error mail without the run link. The link saves minutes per incident.
- Terminating with Succeeded in the Catch scope. The run history then hides the failure.
- Putting a Terminate action inside the Try scope. Terminate ends the whole run at once, so the Catch scope never runs.

=== Testing ===
- Change the URI to a non-existing address and run the flow. You should get one mail with the link.
- Open the link from the mail, it must open the failed run directly.
- Point the URI at an endpoint that returns HTTP 500 and check that the error text in the mail shows the status code.

Document libraries grow forever unless someone cleans them. This flow runs on the first day of each month, selects files whose last modification is older than 730 days, and moves them one by one into an Archive library on the same site. The move uses the SharePoint REST method moveto with flags=0 so that nothing is overwritten, and the item ID in the new name prevents collisions. A summary mail lists the counts and the files that could not be moved.

=== Flow definition (JSON) ===
{
  "properties": {
    "connectionReferences": {
      "shared_office365": {
        "runtimeSource": "embedded",
        "connection": {
          "connectionReferenceLogicalName": "contoso_sharedoffice365_a1b2c"
        },
        "api": {
          "name": "shared_office365"
        }
      },
      "shared_sharepointonline": {
        "runtimeSource": "embedded",
        "connection": {
          "connectionReferenceLogicalName": "contoso_sharedsharepointonline_a1b2c"
        },
        "api": {
          "name": "shared_sharepointonline"
        }
      }
    },
    "definition": {
      "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Logic/schemas/2016-06-01/workflowdefinition.json#",
      "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
      "parameters": {
        "$connections": {
          "defaultValue": {},
          "type": "Object"
        },
        "$authentication": {
          "defaultValue": {},
          "type": "SecureObject"
        },
        "LibraryOwner (contoso_LibraryOwner)": {
          "defaultValue": "projects-admin@contoso.example",
          "type": "String",
          "metadata": {
            "schemaName": "contoso_LibraryOwner"
          }
        }
      },
      "triggers": {
        "First_day_of_month": {
          "type": "Recurrence",
          "recurrence": {
            "frequency": "Month",
            "interval": 1,
            "schedule": {
              "monthDays": [
                1
              ],
              "hours": [
                "3"
              ],
              "minutes": [
                0
              ]
            },
            "timeZone": "W. Europe Standard Time"
          }
        }
      },
      "actions": {
        "Init_archived": {
          "type": "InitializeVariable",
          "runAfter": {},
          "inputs": {
            "variables": [
              {
                "name": "Archived",
                "type": "array",
                "value": []
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "Init_failed": {
          "type": "InitializeVariable",
          "runAfter": {
            "Init_archived": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          },
          "inputs": {
            "variables": [
              {
                "name": "Failed",
                "type": "array",
                "value": []
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "Old_files": {
          "type": "OpenApiConnection",
          "inputs": {
            "host": {
              "connectionName": "shared_sharepointonline",
              "operationId": "GetFileItems",
              "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_sharepointonline"
            },
            "parameters": {
              "dataset": "https://contoso.sharepoint.example/sites/Projects",
              "table": "Project Files",
              "$filter": "@concat('Modified lt ''', formatDateTime(addDays(utcNow(), -730), 'yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssZ'), '''')",
              "$orderby": "Modified asc",
              "$top": 500
            },
            "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
          },
          "runAfter": {
            "Init_failed": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          },
          "runtimeConfiguration": {
            "paginationPolicy": {
              "minimumItemCount": 2000
            }
          }
        },
        "For_each_file": {
          "type": "Foreach",
          "foreach": "@body('Old_files')?['value']",
          "runAfter": {
            "Old_files": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          },
          "runtimeConfiguration": {
            "concurrency": {
              "repetitions": 1
            }
          },
          "actions": {
            "Move_to_archive": {
              "type": "OpenApiConnection",
              "inputs": {
                "host": {
                  "connectionName": "shared_sharepointonline",
                  "operationId": "HttpRequest",
                  "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_sharepointonline"
                },
                "parameters": {
                  "dataset": "https://contoso.sharepoint.example/sites/Projects",
                  "parameters/method": "POST",
                  "parameters/uri": "@concat('/_api/web/GetFileByServerRelativeUrl(''/sites/Projects/', replace(item()?['{FullPath}'], '''', ''''''), ''')/moveto(newurl=''/sites/Projects/Archive/', item()?['ID'], '-', replace(item()?['{Name}'], '''', ''''''), ''',flags=0)')",
                  "parameters/headers": {
                    "accept": "application/json;odata=nometadata"
                  }
                },
                "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
              },
              "runAfter": {}
            },
            "Remember_moved": {
              "type": "AppendToArrayVariable",
              "runAfter": {
                "Move_to_archive": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": {
                "name": "Archived",
                "value": "@item()?['{FullPath}']"
              }
            },
            "Remember_failed": {
