          }
        },
        "Summary_mail": {
          "type": "OpenApiConnection",
          "inputs": {
            "host": {
              "connectionName": "shared_office365",
              "operationId": "SendEmailV2",
              "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_office365"
            },
            "parameters": {
              "emailMessage/To": "@parameters('LibraryOwner (contoso_LibraryOwner)')",
              "emailMessage/Subject": "@concat('Archive run: ', length(variables('Archived')), ' files moved, ', length(variables('Failed')), ' failed')",
              "emailMessage/Body": "@concat('<p>Moved: ', length(variables('Archived')), '</p><p>Failed: ', length(variables('Failed')), '</p><p>Failed files:<br>', if(empty(variables('Failed')), 'none', join(variables('Failed'), '<br>')), '</p>')",
              "emailMessage/Importance": "Normal"
            },
            "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
          },
          "runAfter": {
            "For_each_file": [
              "Succeeded",
              "Failed"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "schemaVersion": "1.0.0.0"
}

=== How to use ===
1. Create the library 'Archive' on the site and make sure the flow account can edit both libraries.
2. Replace the site address, library name and the server-relative prefix /sites/Projects in the URI expression.
3. First run with the filter set to a small test library and a threshold of -1 day so that you see the behaviour on a few files.
4. Add a retention label or a 'Moved on' column in a later version if compliance needs a trail inside SharePoint.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Using moveto with flags=1. That overwrites existing files in the target and can destroy data.
- Forgetting to double apostrophes in file names. A name like O'Brien.docx breaks the REST URL without the replace function.
- Expecting subfolders to be created. moveto does not create folders, so this example uses one flat Archive library.
- Running in parallel while appending to variables. The sequential setting avoids lost updates.
- Filtering on Created instead of Modified. Old files that are still edited would be archived.

=== Testing ===
- Create three old test files and one name with an apostrophe and run once.
- Check the Archive library names and that the original file is gone from the source.
- Make one target name exist already and check that it lands in the failed list.

Guest accounts pile up. This flow calls Microsoft Graph with the HTTP action and an app registration, follows paging with the pagination setting, and finds guests that were created more than 90 days ago and have no sign-in for 90 days. It saves the full list as CSV and mails the first 20 rows. It only reports; deleting or blocking guests should stay a human decision or a separate, approved flow.

=== Flow definition (JSON) ===
