            "from": "@body('List_guests')?['value']",
            "where": "@and(less(ticks(item()?['createdDateTime']), ticks(addDays(utcNow(), -90))), if(empty(item()?['signInActivity']?['lastSignInDateTime']), true, less(ticks(item()?['signInActivity']?['lastSignInDateTime']), ticks(addDays(utcNow(), -90)))))"
          }
        },
        "Csv": {
          "type": "Table",
          "runAfter": {
            "Stale_guests": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          },
          "inputs": {
            "from": "@body('Stale_guests')",
            "format": "CSV",
            "columns": [
              {
                "header": "DisplayName",
                "value": "@item()?['displayName']"
              },
              {
                "header": "Mail",
                "value": "@item()?['mail']"
              },
              {
                "header": "Created",
                "value": "@item()?['createdDateTime']"
              },
              {
                "header": "LastSignIn",
                "value": "@coalesce(item()?['signInActivity']?['lastSignInDateTime'], 'never')"
              },
              {
                "header": "Id",
                "value": "@item()?['id']"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "Save_csv": {
          "type": "OpenApiConnection",
          "inputs": {
            "host": {
              "connectionName": "shared_sharepointonline",
              "operationId": "CreateFile",
              "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_sharepointonline"
            },
            "parameters": {
              "dataset": "https://contoso.sharepoint.example/sites/Governance",
              "folderPath": "/Reports",
              "name": "@concat('stale-guests-', formatDateTime(utcNow(), 'yyyy-MM-dd'), '.csv')",
              "body": "@body('Csv')"
            },
            "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
          },
          "runAfter": {
            "Csv": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          }
        },
        "Top_20": {
          "type": "Compose",
          "runAfter": {
            "Save_csv": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          },
          "inputs": "@take(body('Stale_guests'), 20)"
        },
        "Html": {
          "type": "Table",
          "inputs": {
            "from": "@outputs('Top_20')",
            "format": "HTML",
            "columns": [
              {
                "header": "DisplayName",
                "value": "@item()?['displayName']"
              },
              {
                "header": "Mail",
                "value": "@item()?['mail']"
              },
              {
                "header": "Created",
                "value": "@item()?['createdDateTime']"
              },
              {
                "header": "LastSignIn",
                "value": "@coalesce(item()?['signInActivity']?['lastSignInDateTime'], 'never')"
              }
            ]
          },
          "runAfter": {
            "Top_20": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          }
        },
        "Mail_owner": {
          "type": "OpenApiConnection",
          "inputs": {
            "host": {
              "connectionName": "shared_office365",
              "operationId": "SendEmailV2",
              "apiId": "/providers/Microsoft.PowerApps/apis/shared_office365"
            },
            "parameters": {
              "emailMessage/To": "@parameters('GovernanceMailbox (contoso_GovernanceMailbox)')",
              "emailMessage/Subject": "@concat('Guest review: ', length(body('Stale_guests')), ' inactive guest accounts')",
              "emailMessage/Body": "@concat('<p>', length(body('Stale_guests')), ' of ', length(body('List_guests')?['value']), ' guests have not signed in for 90 days or never signed in.</p>', body('Html'), '<p>The full list is in the Reports library.</p>')",
              "emailMessage/Importance": "Normal"
            },
            "authentication": "@parameters('$authentication')"
          },
          "runAfter": {
            "Html": [
              "Succeeded"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "schemaVersion": "1.0.0.0"
}

=== How to use ===
1. Register an app in Microsoft Entra ID with the application permissions User.Read.All and AuditLog.Read.All and grant admin consent. The sign-in activity property needs at least Entra ID P1.
2. Store the client secret in Azure Key Vault and use an environment variable of type secret that points to it. Never paste the secret into the flow. Prefer a certificate or managed identity where your design allows it.
3. Create the three environment variables TenantId, GraphClientId and GraphClientSecret, and the library Reports.
4. Run once and compare the count with the Entra admin center, then decide which follow-up (access review, block sign-in) fits your policy.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Requesting more than 120 users per page together with signInActivity. Graph limits the page size in that case, so the example uses 100.
- Comparing date strings directly. Different fractional seconds break string comparison; ticks() converts both to numbers.
- Giving the app the Directory.ReadWrite.All permission 'to be safe'. The report needs read permissions only.
- Forgetting that the HTTP action is a premium connector and needs a matching licence.
- Treating 'never signed in' as inactive for guests who were invited yesterday. The 90-day creation filter prevents that.

=== Testing ===
- Run the flow and check the HTTP output for @odata.nextLink; the pagination setting should merge the pages.
- Create a test guest and confirm it is not in the report during the first 90 days.
- Check that the CSV opens correctly and does not contain secrets or tokens.

Instead of one reminder email per task, owners get one digest per day. The flow loads all overdue tasks with a server-side filter, extracts the assignee emails, removes duplicates with union(), and then, for each owner, filters the in-memory list, builds an HTML table with days overdue, and sends the mail. The PMO gets a one-line summary. Because unassigned tasks have no email, they are excluded from the digests and appear only in the PMO count.

