=== How to use ===
1. Adapt site, list name and the columns Status, DueDate and AssignedTo (person column). Choice column filters use the text value.
2. Create an environment variable PmoMailbox and turn the flow on with a service account that can read the list.
3. Run it manually and check the owner list in the Unique_owners output.
4. Optionally add a second digest for the manager level by grouping on a department column.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Calling Get items once per owner. That multiplies requests; one query plus Filter array is faster and avoids throttling.
- Forgetting pagination. Without the threshold only 100 items are read by default.
- Dividing ticks incorrectly. One day equals 864000000000 ticks (100-nanosecond units).
- Using high concurrency for mails. Five parallel iterations are enough and keep you below mail limits.
- Mailing people who left the company. Check the account status or use a group in test mode first.

=== Testing ===
- Set one task overdue for two different people and run the flow. Each person gets only their own table.
- Complete all tasks and check that the run ends with Succeeded and no mail is sent.
- Check the day count against a date calculation by hand.
